{"kind": "chat_performance", "workload": "python", "repeat": 2, "prompt": "Write a Python function that parses timestamped log lines, groups errors by hour, and returns the five most frequent messages. Explain edge cases and include tests.", "input_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 7734, 264, 12654, 709, 421, 68434, 11112, 290, 1433, 4965, 11, 5038, 5787, 539, 6258, 11, 321, 4523, 279, 4097, 1379, 20125, 6397, 13, 79091, 6607, 4886, 321, 2830, 6813, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "prompt_tokens": 43, "output_tokens": 256, "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\n\ndef parse_log_line(line: str) -> Optional[Tuple[datetime, str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a single log line and return (timestamp, message) if valid.\n    \n    Expected format: [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS] message\n    Example: [2023-10-05 14:30:45] ERROR: Connection timeout\n    \n    Returns None if the line cannot be parsed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not line or not line.strip():\n        return None\n    \n    # Match timestamp in brackets followed by the message\n    pattern = r'^\\[(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} \\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2})\\]\\s*(.*)$'\n    match = re.match(pattern, line.strip())\n    \n    if not match:\n        return None\n    \n    timestamp_str = match.group(1)\n    message = match.group(2).strip()\n    \n    try:\n        timestamp = datetime.strptime(timestamp_str, '%Y-%m", "input_sha256": "ed3cc12c1c494580eaed3e90d72603925183e04858c5e3cb4544467f5508d4ce", "output_sha256": "acd59b9b42f28dc06ad6ba2af44ff21fb16a8686d769f3ae11f0eb08f7b76179", "ttft_seconds": 1.2879085093736649, "elapsed_seconds": 14.373786851763725, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 43, "prompt_ms": 1236.6, "prompt_per_token_ms": 28.758, "prompt_per_second": 34.8, "predicted_n": 256, "predicted_ms": 13136.0, "predicted_per_token_ms": 51.312, "predicted_per_second": 19.5, "draft_n": 0, "draft_n_accepted"